    <content type="html">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"&gt;&lt;title&gt;Market Theses · 2026-08-28 · MIXED — Meta's $17B Settlement and Ongoing Legal Overhang&lt;/title&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#f6f7f9;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"&gt;&lt;div style="max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px;"&gt;&lt;div style="background:#ffffff;padding:28px 24px;color:#1a1d24;"&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 20px 0;"&gt;&lt;h1 style="font-size:22px;color:#1a1d24;margin:0;"&gt;Market Theses&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:4px;"&gt;2026-08-28 &amp;middot; Morning Brief&lt;span style="display:inline-block;border:1px solid #b8860b;color:#b8860b;border-radius:999px;padding:1px 8px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.04em;margin-left:8px;"&gt;MIXED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style="color:#b8860b;font-size:15px;margin:24px 0 10px 0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;"&gt;Focus&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t0" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Meta's $17B Settlement and Ongoing Legal Overhang&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Meta agreed to pay up to $17.1B to settle a multi-state social media addiction lawsuit, the largest such settlement, but ongoing litigation, EU regulatory escalation, and challenges enforcing teen safeguards continue to weigh on the company.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/us/meta-settles-with-us-states-over-social-media-harms-2026-08-26/" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t1" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;AI Infrastructure Boom Reaffirmed&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#1a7f37;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▲ bull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; Nvidia earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Nvidia's blockbuster earnings and guidance, along with Salesforce's AI-driven beat and cybersecurity earnings from CrowdStrike and Okta, confirmed that hyperscale AI capex and enterprise AI adoption remain robust. The results lifted the entire tech sector, with Nvidia adding over $400B in market cap and the Nasdaq 100 rising 1.1%.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/27/nvidia-nvda-q2-earnings.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;CNBC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style="color:#b8860b;font-size:15px;margin:24px 0 10px 0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;"&gt;Market in one paragraph&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;MIXED — Markets are caught between two powerful forces. A blockbuster tech earnings cycle—Nvidia's $400B market cap surge, Salesforce's 22% rally, and record cybersecurity results from CrowdStrike and Okta—is driving a risk-on rotation into AI and software stocks, reinforced by family office bullishness and falling yields. Simultaneously, escalating US-Canada trade war (tariffs, Lake Ontario renaming), persistent geopolitical flashpoints (Strait of Hormuz tanker attacks, CIA Moscow warning, Qatar-Iran mediation), and a hawkish Fed (Hammack calling for rate hikes) are capping risk appetite and keeping safe-haven demand alive. Meta's $17B social-media settlement adds a legal overhang, while a disastrous Himalayan flood deepens human and infrastructure toll. The net picture is a MIXED regime where tech momentum contests with macro and geopolitical headwinds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size:13px;color:#5a5f6b;margin:0 0 4px 0;"&gt;S&amp;amp;P 500 7,731 (+0.7%) · Nasdaq 26,541 (+1.6%) · Dow 53,569 (+0.2%) · 10Y UST 4.67% (+1bp) · WTI $84 (+2.2%) · Gold $4,656 (-0.5%) · BTC $80,349 (+1.7%) · DXY 99.1 (-0.0%) · USD/JPY 159.4 (+0.0%)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;Quotes as of 2026-08-27 23:30 UTC&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="color:#b8860b;font-size:15px;margin:24px 0 10px 0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;"&gt;By section&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 8px 0;color:#1a1d24;"&gt;Macro&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t9" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Geopolitical risk from Iran/Hormuz and Russia-Ukraine escalation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Tensions remain elevated with a 95% drop in Strait of Hormuz traffic from the US-Israel war on Iran, Putin escalating in Ukraine, and Russia launching hybrid attacks on Europe. The CIA director's reported Moscow trip aimed to ease tensions, but uncertainty persists, boosting oil prices and safe-haven demand.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/27/how-a-95-percent-drop-in-hormuz-traffic-changed-global-shipping" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t17" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Himalayan glacial flood disaster hits Nepal-Tibet border&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;A glacial-lake outburst flood along the Nepal-Tibet border has caused hundreds of deaths and over 1,400 missing, destroying infrastructure and disrupting cross-border trade. The disaster raises concerns about climate-driven risks and Chinese infrastructure vulnerability.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-27/tibet-mudslide-engulfs-complex-at-china-s-gateway-to-nepal" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t48" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;European political risk from France budget showdown and Orban collapse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;France faces a risky budget battle that could strain the euro and French bonds, while Hungary's Orban sees his EU influence collapse. These events, combined with NATO defense spending pressure, create political uncertainty for European assets.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-26/french-showdown-over-next-budget-will-be-macron-s-riskiest-yet" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 8px 0;color:#1a1d24;"&gt;Equities&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t2" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Shein's IPO Valuation Collapse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Shein's long-awaited Hong Kong IPO priced at a fraction of its $100B peak valuation, raising $1.73B at ~$26.5B, reflecting slowed growth, failed US/UK listings, and FTC investigation. The drastic markdown sent a bearish signal for high-growth private-company valuations.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-23/shein-seeks-up-to-1-8-billion-in-long-awaited-hong-kong-ipo" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t3" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Consumer Discretionary Earnings Divergence&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; mix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Retail and consumer stocks showed starkly divergent results: Gap jumped 12% on a new CEO, Abercrombie raised guidance, but Nike is on pace for its worst year since 1998, Best Buy fell despite a beat, HP dropped 8.9% on PC demand worries, and Wendy's fell 13% on a failed bid.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/27/gap-q2-2026-earnings.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;CNBC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t4" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;AI Chip Competition and China Geopolitics Heat Up&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; mix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; Nvidia earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Nvidia resumed H200 chip sales to China, but a US probe into smuggling and OpenAI's claim that its new 'Jalapeno' chip outperforms Nvidia highlight intensifying competition. Huawei's Ascend push in Egypt and Nvidia's support for Chinese AI models also complicate the landscape.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-26/nvidia-steps-back-into-china-market-with-first-h200-chip-sales" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 8px 0;color:#1a1d24;"&gt;Rates &amp;amp; FX&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t6" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;US-Canada trade war escalation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; US-Canada trade war&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;The U.S. and Canada are locked in an escalating trade dispute, with new tariffs, retaliatory actions, and symbolic gestures like renaming Lake Ontario. The conflict threatens North American supply chains and corporate investment, though some analysts see a path to compromise.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/27/trump-canada-lake-america-ontario.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;CNBC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t11" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Geopolitical and Trade Tensions Weigh on Markets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; US-Canada trade war&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Escalating US-Canada trade disputes, Middle East tensions, and a VIX curve bump signaled rising anxiety. The TSX fell 0.4% from record highs, and Barclays warned that voter backlash against AI data-center buildouts could hurt the AI trade.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://moztako.me/trump-tariffs-on-canadian-automobiles/" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Moztako&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t12" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;US Fiscal and Treasury Intervention Skepticism&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#b42318;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▼ bear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Rising US federal debt, warnings from Fed officials and investors, and skepticism about Treasury Secretary Bessent's bond buyback program keep long-term Treasury yields elevated despite temporary buyback-driven squeezes.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-26/bessent-s-treasury-twist-makes-november-refunding-a-wall-street-wildcard" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 8px 0;color:#1a1d24;"&gt;Commodities&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t13" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Strait of Hormuz: Reopening Hopes vs. Persistent Attacks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; mix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; Strait of Hormuz&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Conflicting signals around the Strait of Hormuz: diplomatic efforts (Iran-Oman talks, Qatari mediation) suggest possible reopening, reducing risk premium, while repeated tanker attacks and US legal escalation keep the geopolitical risk elevated. The net effect is a volatile, mixed oil price outlook.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-25/iran-oman-push-talks-for-interim-reopening-of-hormuz-strait" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t20" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Gold and Bitcoin Scarcity Trade Draws $7B&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#1a7f37;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▲ bull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Gold and Bitcoin ETFs attracted $7 billion in combined inflows as the 'scarcity trade' resurges. Gold outperformed Bitcoin year-to-date (+7% vs -10%), indicating a preference for hard-asset scarcity over crypto.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-26/bitcoin-and-gold-etfs-draw-7-billion-as-scarcity-trade-surges" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t21" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Natural Gas Emerges as Key European Inflation Risk&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#1a7f37;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▲ bull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Natural gas prices have eclipsed oil as the dominant inflation risk for European sovereign debt. Investors should watch TTF benchmarks more closely than Brent for euro-area rate paths.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-26/natural-gas-eclipses-oil-as-key-inflation-risk-for-european-debt" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 8px 0;color:#1a1d24;"&gt;Crypto&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t7" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Sovereign and Geopolitical Adoption&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#1a7f37;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▲ bull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; Crypto regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;State actors like Iran and UAE are integrating crypto into their economic and trade strategies, signaling legitimization. Iran launches Bitcoin-backed insurance and demands crypto tolls; UAE sheikh backs Trump's crypto bank.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/27/uae-spy-sheikh-trump-family-crypto-bank.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t41" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Favorable US Regulatory Signals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#1a7f37;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▲ bull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; Crypto regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Recent regulatory developments, including Trump Jr. urging state AGs not to fight prediction markets, SEC proposing new exemption framework, and progress on custody rules, create a supportive environment for crypto.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/27/trump-jr-told-gop-state-attorneys-general-dont-fight-prediction-markets-nyt-reports.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 14px 0;"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html#thesis:t46" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;"&gt;Bitcoin-Backed Mortgages Drive Real-World Adoption&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:#1a7f37;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; ▲ bull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#5a5f6b;font-size:12px;"&gt; &amp;middot; Crypto regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;color:#1a1d24;margin-top:2px;"&gt;The launch of Bitcoin-backed mortgages by Coinbase and Better Mortgage, with $260M waitlist demand, signals growing real-world utility for Bitcoin as collateral, boosting bullish sentiment.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;margin-top:2px;"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://news.bitcoin.com/featured/coinbase-better-open-bitcoin-mortgages-after-260m-waitlist-demand/" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;35&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style="color:#b8860b;font-size:15px;margin:24px 0 10px 0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;"&gt;Week ahead&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Aug 27-29&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;middot; Jackson Hole symposium — 'Financial Innovation: Payments and Policy' &amp;middot; high&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sep 2&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;middot; Broadcom Q3 FY26 earnings (after close) — AI-semi read-through &amp;middot; med&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sep 4&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;middot; August jobs report (8:30 ET) &amp;middot; high&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sep 11&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;middot; August CPI (8:30 ET) — last inflation print before the FOMC &amp;middot; high&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sep 15-16&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;middot; FOMC meeting — rate decision + dot plot Sep 16 (14:00 ET) &amp;middot; high&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sep 18&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;middot; Quarterly triple witching — index options/futures expiry &amp;middot; med&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style="color:#b8860b;font-size:15px;margin:24px 0 10px 0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;"&gt;Research desk&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:14px;"&gt;AI infrastructure supply-demand imbalance enabling pricing power across components and services&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;"&gt;43 reports · 14 firms &amp;middot; &lt;span style="color:#b8860b;"&gt;consensus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:14px;"&gt;AI-driven demand boosting investment across tech supply chain with data center infrastructure strain&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;"&gt;39 reports · 7 firms &amp;middot; &lt;span style="color:#b8860b;"&gt;consensus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:14px;"&gt;China consumer demand weakness&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;"&gt;35 reports · 10 firms &amp;middot; &lt;span style="color:#b8860b;"&gt;consensus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:28px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid #e3e5ea;font-size:12px;color:#5a5f6b;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/views/2026-08-28.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Open full edition&lt;/a&gt; &amp;middot; &lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/indicators/posture.html" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;Indicators&lt;/a&gt; &amp;middot; &lt;a href="https://stevensshi.github.io/market-view/feed.xml" style="color:#b8860b;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;"&gt;RSS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p style="margin:10px 0 0 0;"&gt;Personal research project. Not investment advice. Sources are linked per evidence point inside the full edition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</content>
